-- title:
--   Lemma 4.2 — an objective $i$-secret event of any probability $\alpha$, independent of a given event
-- statement:
--   Let $(\Omega,\mathcal B,(\mathcal J_i),(p_i))$ be a randomizing structure for a finite set $N$ of players satisfying Assumption II. Then for every player $i$, every event $B\in\mathcal B$ and every $\alpha\in[0,1]$ there is an event $A$ that is
--
--   1. **$i$-secret**: $A\in\mathcal J_i$ and $p_j(A\cap C)=p_j(A)p_j(C)$ for every $j\ne i$ and every $C$ in the $\sigma$-field generated by the $\mathcal J_k$, $k\ne i$;
--   2. **objective with probability $\alpha$**: $p_j(A)=\alpha$ for every player $j$;
--   3. **independent of $B$**: $p_j(A\cap B)=p_j(A)\,p_j(B)$ for every player $j$.
--
--   Intuitively, each player owns an objective roulette wheel that he can spin in secret. In the proof of Proposition 6.1 the lemma is used twice: to cut a subjective event of player 1 down to a prescribed size inside $\mathcal J_1$, and to produce player 2's objective secret randomization of small probability.
--
--   **Formalization Note** Assumption II is a hypothesis (the paper derives the lemma from it by Lemma 7.1 with $\mathcal R=\mathcal R_i$ and $l=1$). Probabilities are compared in $[0,\infty]$, with $\alpha$ embedded as `ENNReal.ofReal α`.
-- source:
--   R. J. Aumann, Subjectivity and Correlation in Randomized Strategies, J. Math. Econ. 1 (1974) 67–96, https://doi.org/10.1016/0304-4068(74)90037-8, p. 77 (PDF p. 11), Lemma 4.2; proof p. 82 (PDF p. 16)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_Aumann1974_ZeroSum_RandomizingStructure

namespace Aumann1974.ZeroSum

open MeasureTheory

/-- **Lemma 4.2** (Aumann 1974, *Subjectivity and Correlation in Randomized Strategies*,
J. Math. Econ. 1, p. 77, PDF p. 11): for any `i` in `N`, any event `B`, and any `α` between `0`
and `1`, there is an objective `i`-secret event with probability `α` that is independent of `B`.

**Formalization Note.** The players form a finite type. Assumption II (standing assumption,
p. 75) is a hypothesis; the paper's proof (p. 82) applies Lemma 7.1 to the roulette `ℛᵢ` it
provides. `B` is any `ℬ`-measurable event. "Objective with probability `α`" is `pⱼ(A) = α` for
every player `j`; "independent of `B`" is `pⱼ(A ∩ B) = pⱼ(A)pⱼ(B)` for every player `j`. -/
theorem objective_secret_event {ι Ω : Type*} [Fintype ι] {mΩ : MeasurableSpace Ω}
    (R : RandomizingStructure ι Ω mΩ) (hII : AssumptionII R)
    (i : ι) (B : Set Ω) (hB : MeasurableSet[mΩ] B)
    (α : ℝ) (hα0 : 0 ≤ α) (hα1 : α ≤ 1) :
    ∃ A : Set Ω, IsSecret R i A ∧ IsObjective R A ∧
      (∀ j, R.p j A = ENNReal.ofReal α) ∧ IsIndependentOf R A B := by sorry

end Aumann1974.ZeroSum
